  "tier": "told-once",
  "plain": "A podcast host, Jesse Michels, tells of a man named Solon Brown who, on March 25, 1948, near Aztec, New Mexico, broke down and cried while talking to a church deacon, Bruce Seer, in a story tied to a reported saucer crash there. Sixty years later, Seer's son told a researcher, Scott Ramsay, that he never forgot that night because it was the first time he had seen a grown man cry. Michels tells it as a sign that whatever Brown saw shook him deeply."
